<h1><span lang="EN-GB">On Rotate/Pan Draw Points</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p>This command is accessible from the <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>viewport context menu &gt; On Rotate/Pan &gt; Draw Points</b></span> or by selecting <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Points</b></span> option in <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>System &gt; Preferences / Display / Rotate/Pan/Zoom</b></span> dialog.</p>
<p class="description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">On Rotate/Pan Draw Points</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command affects visualisation of scan data and meshes in the scene during rotate, pan, and zoom actions and is related to the appearance of objects. Selecting this command will cause KUBE to display objects as points during rotate, pan, and zoom. Number of displayed points depends on what command is selected (Custom, Less, Normal, More) and the settings from</span> <u><span lang="EN-GB"><a href="Display_Settings_-_On_Rotate_Pan.htm">Preferences / Display</a></span></u> <span lang="EN-GB">dialog.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is equivalent to the</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Points</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">option in</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Draw</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">group from</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Preferences / Display / Rotate/Pan/Zoom</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">dialog. This mode is by default and is not stored so next time when you run KUBE</span> <span class="Mode">Draw Points</span> <span lang="EN-GB">will be used.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
